"\n" [:option {:value "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "3"} "1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "4"} "1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "9"} "1928 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "10"} "1932 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "11"} "1936 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "12"} "1948 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "13"} "1952 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "14"} "1956 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/SWM'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Swimming at the 2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July –  4 August 2012"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "32"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/855"} "London Aquatics Centre, Olympic Park, Stratford, London"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Swimming was held at the newly constructed Aquatics Centre in the Olympic Park, although the open water swims were held in at The Serpentine, the eastern part of a lake in Hyde Park. The sport was again highlighted by the presence of " [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"] ", who had won eight gold medals at the Beijing Olympics, and came to London having won 16 medals in all. He was not quite as dominant in London, winning six medals, and four gold medals, but this brought his overall totals to 22 medals and 14 golds, both all-time Olympic records. There was no change to the swimming program since the 2008 Olympics, with men and women both contesting 17 events, 16 in the pool and the open-water swim."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The United States was the dominant nation, winning 16 of 34 gold medals, and 31 medals in all. Phelps won the most medals by any swimmer, while on the women’s side, Americans " [:a {:href "/athletes/126679"} "Missy Franklin"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/115730"} "Allison Schmitt"] " won five medals, with Franklin winning four golds and Schmitt three. In the men’s open-water swim Tunisia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/93816"} "Oussama Mellouli"] " won the gold medal. He also won a bronze medal in the pool in the 1,500 freestyle, an event he had won in 2008, making him the first swimmer to win gold medals both in the pool and open-water events."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Multiple world records were set in London swimming, which reversed the trend of the last few years. Beijing had seen the world record list assaulted as swimmers used skinsuits made from new fabrics and which greatly decreased drag in the water. These were banned after the 2008 Olympics and with the return to what are termed textile suits, world records had been dearly sought since 2008. But the level of competition and the hyper-fast London pool contributed to numerous changes in the world lists."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322275"} "50 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "2 –  3 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "58"] "\n" [:td {} "51"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322179"} "100 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 July –  1 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "56"] "\n" [:td {} "49"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322083"} "200 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "29 – 30 July 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "40"] "\n" [:td {} "31"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322000"} "400 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "28 July 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n" [:td {} "23"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322337"} "1,500 metres Freestyle, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "3 –  4 August 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "31"] "\n" [:td {} "25"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322069"} "4 × 100 metres Freestyle Relay, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "29 July 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "71"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322165"} "4 × 200 metres Freestyle Relay, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 July 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "73"] "\n" [:td {} "16"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322095"} "100 metres Backstroke, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "29 – 30 July 2012"] "\n" [:td {} "43"] "\n" [:td {} "33"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/322239"